nt-grade access still works. That is only one deal.\n- I have no data on leverage, credit ratings or debt headroom. I can't say whether Pellham could replace its failed equity raise with debt without breaching rating thresholds.\n\n**Equity**\n- Pellham Power withdrew a C$2.4B equity raise after demand fell short.\n- Two other utility share offerings were cut back in size in Q3 2026.\n- I found no data on equity valuations or on how much of each plan was meant to be equity-funded.\n\n**By company**\n- **Norvane:** capex is planned up 12%. Its bond deal makes the plan look financeable mainly through debt.\n- **Pellham:** capex is planned up 18%. It is the weak point and is treating its plan as not fully financeable now. It is cutting 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and deferring two substation programmes until financing improves. It is also the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria.\n\n**For equipment demand:** assume the sector's 2027 capex is only partly financed. Pellham's order cut is a concrete downside, while Norvane's orders are intact.\n\nSources are the n5 (debt) and n6 (equity) results: n5.r1, n6.r1.","ttft_ms":4295,"type":"result","duration_ms":32111,"uuid":"8bf0ff22-a330-4820-ac70-edefb18bfa0d","ttft_stream_ms":3797,"time_to_request_ms":180,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":17,"system_prompt":28,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":6,"input_attachments":40,"input_hooks":6,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":6,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":12,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":10,"request_announcements":10,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":7,"tool_schema_build":7,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_build":16},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":33,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":64,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":186,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":112,"process_rss_m